==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|amāta||[[loved]], [[beloved]]}}; feminine perfect passive participle of {{m|la|amāre||love}}. It can also be interpreted as the feminine form of the saint's name {{m|la|Amātus}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|s}}

# {{given name|en|female|from=Latin}}; always rare in English.
# {{lb|en|Roman mythology}} The wife of [[Latinus]] and the mother of [[Lavinia]].

